# Line endings are normalised so that a fact measured on one machine reproduces
# on another. Without this, a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true) holds CRLF
# while git — and CI on ubuntu-latest — store LF, and `wc -c` over the same
# commit returns 142,752 bytes on one and 139,253 on the other. That divergence
# is not theoretical: it put a wrong payload figure in the fact panel and made a
# release guard disagree with CI about whether the backlog was up to date.
#
# Prefer invariance over per-platform branching: a value that is the same
# everywhere needs no adaptation.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary content must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
